        },
        "value": {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Community colleges should expand freshman learning communities when degree gains outweigh their added education cost.",
          "language": {
            "$bytes": "090adac0fca4822e8e719263e67620ec"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "property": {
          "$bytes": "9b1f76ff9711404c861e59dc3fa7d037"
        },
        "value": {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "At Kingsborough, a one-semester learning community raised six-year degree attainment by 4.6 percentage points in a randomized study. Its $3,580 higher education cost per program member and single-college scope make broader expansion a contestable policy judgment.",
          "language": {
            "$bytes": "090adac0fca4822e8e719263e67620ec"
          }
        }
      },
